  "query": "The problem of mutual payment of wages arises in multi‑party cooperation and mutual labor. For example, carpenters, electricians, painters, and other trades form a mutual‑aid group to complete each household’s renovation together. Because the amount of labor differs across trades, a fair standard of mutual payment is needed to balance everyone’s interests. The work_days.csv file records their arrangement. Each row corresponds to a homeowner and each column to a worker; each entry shows how many days a given worker spent renovating that homeowner’s home. The dataset may include many participants (e.g., 120 or more). Each worker contributes exactly 10 work days in total across all projects, including their own home renovation. To set the wage scale, the daily wage of the first worker listed in the file (e.g., the Carpenter) is fixed at 60.00 yuan. Determine the daily wages for all remaining workers so that, for every participant, their total income from working on others’ homes equals their total expenditure for work performed at their own home.\n",
